# Narrow types — only what is used

Components, pages, hooks params, and helpers must type **only the fields they read or write**. Do not pass the full entity type when a subset is enough.

Prefer `Pick<Entity, "field" | ...>` (or an equivalent object with `Entity["field"]` types) so field types stay tied to the schema.

```tsx
// ❌ BAD — forces every Project field even if unused
type ProjectLinkProps = {
	project: Project
}

export function ProjectLink(props: ProjectLinkProps) {
	return <Link href={`/projects/${props.project.id}`}>{props.project.name}</Link>
}

// ✅ GOOD — only id and name
type ProjectLinkProps = {
	project: Pick<Project, "id" | "name">
}

export function ProjectLink(props: ProjectLinkProps) {
	return <Link href={`/projects/${props.project.id}`}>{props.project.name}</Link>
}
```

```tsx
// ❌ BAD
type OnDropArgs = {
	project: Project
}

// ✅ GOOD
type OnDropArgs = {
	id: Project["id"]
}
```

When the consumer needs more fields later, widen the `Pick` (or args) at that call site — do not type unused fields “just in case”.

# Parent props compose child props

Export each component’s `{ComponentName}Props` type. A parent must **import** the child’s props type and build its own with `Pick` / `Omit` / intersection — never redeclare the same fields the child already typed.

```tsx
// project-link.tsx
export type ProjectLinkProps = {
	project: Pick<Project, "id" | "name">
}

export function ProjectLink(props: ProjectLinkProps) {
	return <Link href={`/projects/${props.project.id}`}>{props.project.name}</Link>
}

// projects-list.tsx
import { ProjectLink, type ProjectLinkProps } from "./project-link"

// ❌ BAD — duplicates the child’s shape
type ProjectsListProps = {
	projects: { id: number; name: string }[]
	onDrop: (id: number) => void
}

// ✅ GOOD — reuses the child’s props type
type ProjectsListProps = {
	projects: ProjectLinkProps["project"][]
	onDrop: (id: ProjectLinkProps["project"]["id"]) => void
}

// ✅ GOOD — parent forwards a slice of child props
type ProjectRowProps = ProjectLinkProps & {
	onDrop: (id: ProjectLinkProps["project"]["id"]) => void
}
```

When the child props change, parents that compose them stay in sync without parallel edits.

# Page config slices

`WithValidConfig` requires a Zod `schema` and validates **only that slice** of `user.config`. Pass a schema with the keys the page uses — not the full `configSchema` — so unrelated invalid keys do not block the page.

On save, PUT only the keys this page updates and merge them into local `user.config` on success.
